3,"Dinka, Southeastern in Australia people group profile | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/11566/AS,"The Southeastern Dinka, also known as the Bor Dinka, speak a dialect of the Dinka language called Southeastern Dinka. This dialect is part of the Nilotic language family, specifically the Eastern Sudanic branch of the Nilo-Saharan languages.","Dinka, Southeastern",Nilo-Saharan
4,Dinka (Southeastern) Language Sample | Language Museum,https://www.language-museum.com/encyclopedia/d/dinka-southeastern.php,"If you want to get a flavour of the Dinka (Southeastern) language, check out a small sample at the Language Museum.Sudan (250,000) - Total (250,000). Classification. Nilo-Saharan | Eastern Sudanic.","Dinka, Southeastern",Nilo-Saharan
5,Dinka language and culture,https://www.lonweb.org/link-dinka.htm,"TWI (SOUTHEASTERN DINKA, Tuic, Bor, Eastern Dinka) Spoken in Sudan. Sudan Hail Mary! Mo, Maria, adom hye wo ma, awurade ka woho, wohyira wo mma mu, na wohyira wo yam aba Yesu.","Dinka, Southeastern",Nilo-Saharan
6,Dinka: Have You Heard Of This Interesting... - Crystal Clear Translation,https://crystalcleartranslation.com/dinka-have-you-heard-of-this-interesting-western-nilotic-language/,"Part of the Nilo-Saharan language family, Dinka, also known as Jieng, is a Western Nilotic language spoken primarily by the Dinka people. In total, there are 1.35 million speakers of the Dinka language, primarily in South Sudan.","Dinka, Southeastern",Nilo-Saharan
