8,Comparing Nilo-Saharan East Africans And West Africans... | MedShun,https://medshun.com/article/are-nilo-saharan-east-africans-or-west-africans,"Some examples of Nilo-Saharan ethnic groups found in East Africa include the Dinka, Nuer, Shilluk, Maasai, Kalenjin, and Luo. These groups have distinct cultural practices, languages, and traditions that are unique to their respective communities.","Dinka, Southeastern",Nilo-Saharan
9,"Nilo-Saharan languages - Diffusion, African, Speakers | Britannica",https://www.britannica.com/topic/Nilo-Saharan-languages/The-diffusion-of-Nilo-Saharan-languages,"The diffusion of Nilo-Saharan languages.In recent times several Nilo-Saharan languages in these areas, such as Fur, Kanuri, and Songhai, became associated with centralized political units whose states formed important chains in trans-Saharan trade routes.","Dinka, Southeastern",Nilo-Saharan
